Code snippet for all the types of hot publishers,

1) Sinks.many():

  a) Multicast(broadcast to all current subscribers)
  Sinks.Many<Integer> sink = Sinks.many()
          .multicast()
          .onBackpressureBuffer();
  
  Flux<Integer> flux = sink.asFlux();
  flux.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub1: " + v));
  sink.tryEmitNext(1);
  flux.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub2: " + v));
  sink.tryEmitNext(2);

  b) Uniucast(only one subscriber allowed)
  Sinks.Many<String> sink = Sinks.many()
          .unicast()
          .onBackpressureBuffer();
  
  Flux<String> flux = sink.asFlux();
  flux.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Receiver: " + v));
  sink.tryEmitNext("A");
  sink.tryEmitNext("B");

  c) Replay (replay history to new subscribers)
  Sinks.Many<Integer> sink = Sinks.many()
          .replay()
          .limit(2); // replay last 2 items
  
  Flux<Integer> flux = sink.asFlux();
  
  sink.tryEmitNext(10);
  sink.tryEmitNext(20);
  sink.tryEmitNext(30);
  flux.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub1: " + v)); // gets 20, 30
  sink.tryEmitNext(40);
  flux.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub2: " + v)); // gets 30, 40

2) ConnectableFlux — Older Hot Publishers

  a) publish() — Hot after connect()
  ConnectableFlux<Integer> hot = Flux.range(1, 5)
          .delayElements(Duration.ofSeconds(1))
          .publish();
  
  hot.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub1: " + v));
  hot.connect(); // start emitting
  Thread.sleep(2500);
  hot.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub2: " + v)); // misses old items
  
  b) replay() — Hot + Replay Cache
  ConnectableFlux<Integer> replay = Flux.range(1, 5)
          .delayElements(Duration.ofMillis(300))
          .replay(2);  // replay last 2 values
  
  replay.connect();
  Thread.sleep(1000);
  replay.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Late Subscriber: " + v)); // gets last 2

3) share() — Hot Publisher with refCount()
Flux<Long> shared = Flux.interval(Duration.ofMillis(500))
        .share();

shared.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub1: " + v));
Thread.sleep(1500);
shared.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub2: " + v)); // misses initial ticks

4) Built-in Hot Source — interval()
Flux<Long> hot = Flux.interval(Duration.ofSeconds(1));
hot.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub1: " + v));
Thread.sleep(3000);
hot.subscribe(v -> System.out.println("Sub2: " + v)); // only future ticks










